{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Database Optimization & Backup Monitor",
  "description": "REQ-52: Database performance optimization, replication, automated backups, connection pooling, index strategy",
  "version": "1.0",
  "priority": "high",

  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "backend/models/**/*.py",
      "backend/database/**/*.py",
      "backend/alembic/versions/**/*.py",
      "backend/database/optimization.py",
      "backend/database/monitoring.py",
      "backend/core/database.py",
      "backend/scripts/backup_database.py",
      "docker-compose.yml",
      "backend/database/connection_pool.py"
    ]
  },

  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "DATABASE OPTIMIZATION & RELIABILITY VALIDATION (REQ-52):\n\n**1. Query Performance Optimization**\n\n1.1 Index Strategy (REQ-52.1):\n   ❌ REJECT: Foreign keys without indexes\n   ❌ REJECT: WHERE clause columns without indexes\n   ❌ REJECT: ORDER BY columns without indexes\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Indexes on all foreign keys\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Composite indexes for multi-column queries\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Unique indexes for unique constraints\n   \n   ```python\n   # BAD - No index\n   class Student(Base):\n       email = Column(String)  # Frequently queried, no index\n   \n   # GOOD - Indexed\n   class Student(Base):\n       email = Column(String, index=True, unique=True)\n       school_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey('schools.id'), index=True)\n       \n       __table_args__ = (\n           Index('idx_student_grade_section', 'grade', 'section'),\n       )\n   ```\n\n1.2 N+1 Query Problem (REQ-52.2):\n   ❌ REJECT: Loop with individual queries\n   ❌ REJECT: Lazy loading in loops\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Eager loading with joinedload/selectinload\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Single query with JOIN when possible\n   \n   ```python\n   # BAD - N+1 problem\n   students = session.query(Student).all()\n   for student in students:\n       print(student.school.name)  # Separate query per student!\n   \n   # GOOD - Eager loading\n   from sqlalchemy.orm import joinedload\n   students = session.query(Student).options(\n       joinedload(Student.school)\n   ).all()\n   for student in students:\n       print(student.school.name)  # No extra queries\n   ```\n\n1.3 Query Result Caching (REQ-52.3):\n   ❌ REJECT: Repeated identical queries without caching\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Redis caching for frequent queries\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Cache invalidation on data updates\n   ✅ REQUIRE: TTL based on data volatility\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Cached query\n   @cache_result(ttl=3600)  # 1 hour cache\n   def get_popular_courses():\n       return session.query(Course).filter(\n           Course.enrollment_count > 1000\n       ).all()\n   ```\n\n**2. Connection Pool Management**\n\n2.1 Connection Pool Configuration (REQ-52.4):\n   ❌ REJECT: Default pool size (too small for 100K users)\n   ❌ REJECT: No pool overflow handling\n   ❌ REJECT: No connection timeout\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Pool size = 20-50 connections\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Max overflow = 10\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Pool pre-ping to detect stale connections\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Connection timeout = 30 seconds\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Optimized pool\n   engine = create_engine(\n       DATABASE_URL,\n       pool_size=30,              # Base connections\n       max_overflow=10,           # Extra during peak\n       pool_pre_ping=True,        # Check before use\n       pool_recycle=3600,         # Recycle after 1 hour\n       connect_args={\n           \"connect_timeout\": 30,\n           \"application_name\": \"kiro_platform\"\n       }\n   )\n   ```\n\n2.2 Connection Leak Detection (REQ-52.5):\n   ❌ REJECT: Sessions not closed properly\n   ❌ REJECT: No context manager for sessions\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Auto-close with context manager\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Connection leak monitoring\n   \n   ```python\n   # BAD - Connection leak risk\n   session = SessionLocal()\n   result = session.query(User).all()\n   # session.close() might be skipped on error!\n   \n   # GOOD - Guaranteed cleanup\n   with SessionLocal() as session:\n       result = session.query(User).all()\n       # Auto-closed even on exception\n   ```\n\n**3. Database Replication & High Availability**\n\n3.1 Master-Replica Setup (REQ-52.6):\n   ❌ REJECT: Single database instance (SPOF)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Master-replica replication (1 master, 2+ replicas)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Read queries → replicas\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Write queries → master\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Automatic failover to replica\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Read/write split\n   class DatabaseRouter:\n       def db_for_read(self):\n           return random.choice(['replica1', 'replica2'])\n       \n       def db_for_write(self):\n           return 'master'\n   \n   # Usage\n   @route_to_replica\n   def get_students():\n       return session.query(Student).all()\n   \n   @route_to_master\n   def create_student(data):\n       session.add(Student(**data))\n       session.commit()\n   ```\n\n3.2 Replication Lag Monitoring (REQ-52.7):\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor replication lag (< 1 second)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Alert if lag > 5 seconds\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Health check endpoint for replication status\n   \n   ```python\n   def check_replication_lag():\n       master_timestamp = get_master_timestamp()\n       replica_timestamp = get_replica_timestamp()\n       lag = master_timestamp - replica_timestamp\n       \n       if lag > 5:\n           alert_ops_team(f\"Replication lag: {lag}s\")\n       \n       return lag\n   ```\n\n**4. Automated Backups**\n\n4.1 Backup Strategy (REQ-52.8):\n   ❌ REJECT: No automated backups\n   ❌ REJECT: Backups without verification\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Daily full backups (2 AM)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Hourly incremental backups\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Backup retention: 30 days full, 7 days incremental\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Automated restore testing (weekly)\n   \n   ```bash\n   # GOOD - Automated backup script\n   #!/bin/bash\n   # Daily at 2 AM via cron\n   \n   TIMESTAMP=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)\n   BACKUP_DIR=\"/backups/postgresql\"\n   \n   # Full backup with compression\n   pg_dump -h localhost -U postgres kiro_db \\\n     | gzip > $BACKUP_DIR/kiro_full_$TIMESTAMP.sql.gz\n   \n   # Verify backup integrity\n   gunzip -t $BACKUP_DIR/kiro_full_$TIMESTAMP.sql.gz\n   \n   # Upload to S3 with encryption\n   aws s3 cp $BACKUP_DIR/kiro_full_$TIMESTAMP.sql.gz \\\n     s3://kiro-backups/db/ --sse AES256\n   \n   # Delete old backups (>30 days)\n   find $BACKUP_DIR -name \"kiro_full_*.sql.gz\" -mtime +30 -delete\n   ```\n\n4.2 Point-in-Time Recovery (REQ-52.9):\n   ✅ REQUIRE: WAL archiving enabled\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Ability to restore to any point in last 7 days\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Documented restore procedure\n   \n   ```sql\n   -- postgresql.conf\n   wal_level = replica\n   archive_mode = on\n   archive_command = 'aws s3 cp %p s3://kiro-backups/wal/%f'\n   ```\n\n**5. Query Performance Monitoring**\n\n5.1 Slow Query Logging (REQ-52.10):\n   ❌ REJECT: No query performance tracking\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Log queries > 1 second\n   ✅ REQUIRE: EXPLAIN ANALYZE for slow queries\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Weekly slow query review\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Query timing middleware\n   from sqlalchemy import event\n   from sqlalchemy.engine import Engine\n   import time\n   \n   @event.listens_for(Engine, \"before_cursor_execute\")\n   def before_cursor_execute(conn, cursor, statement, parameters, context, executemany):\n       conn.info.setdefault('query_start_time', []).append(time.time())\n   \n   @event.listens_for(Engine, \"after_cursor_execute\")\n   def after_cursor_execute(conn, cursor, statement, parameters, context, executemany):\n       total = time.time() - conn.info['query_start_time'].pop()\n       if total > 1.0:  # Slow query threshold\n           logger.warning(f\"Slow query ({total:.2f}s): {statement[:200]}\")\n   ```\n\n5.2 Database Metrics (REQ-52.11):\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor active connections\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor query throughput (QPS)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor cache hit ratio (> 95%)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor table bloat\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Monitor index usage\n   \n   ```sql\n   -- Check cache hit ratio\n   SELECT \n     sum(heap_blks_read) as heap_read,\n     sum(heap_blks_hit) as heap_hit,\n     sum(heap_blks_hit) / (sum(heap_blks_hit) + sum(heap_blks_read)) AS ratio\n   FROM pg_statio_user_tables;\n   \n   -- Check unused indexes\n   SELECT \n     schemaname, tablename, indexname, idx_scan\n   FROM pg_stat_user_indexes\n   WHERE idx_scan = 0\n   ORDER BY pg_relation_size(indexrelid) DESC;\n   ```\n\n**6. Data Integrity & Consistency**\n\n6.1 Transaction Management (REQ-52.12):\n   ❌ REJECT: Long-running transactions (> 30s)\n   ❌ REJECT: Missing transaction for related operations\n   ✅ REQUIRE: ACID compliance for all writes\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Proper isolation levels\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Deadlock detection and retry\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Transactional integrity\n   from sqlalchemy.exc import OperationalError\n   import time\n   \n   def create_exam_attempt_with_retry(student_id, exam_id, max_retries=3):\n       for attempt in range(max_retries):\n           try:\n               with session.begin():  # Auto-commit/rollback\n                   # Create attempt\n                   attempt = ExamAttempt(\n                       student_id=student_id,\n                       exam_id=exam_id\n                   )\n                   session.add(attempt)\n                   \n                   # Update student stats (must be atomic)\n                   student = session.query(Student).filter_by(\n                       id=student_id\n                   ).with_for_update().one()  # Row lock\n                   student.exam_count += 1\n                   \n                   return attempt\n           except OperationalError as e:\n               if \"deadlock\" in str(e) and attempt < max_retries - 1:\n                   time.sleep(0.1 * (attempt + 1))  # Exponential backoff\n                   continue\n               raise\n   ```\n\n**7. Schema Migration Safety**\n\n7.1 Alembic Migrations (REQ-52.13):\n   ❌ REJECT: Direct schema changes in production\n   ❌ REJECT: Destructive migrations without backup\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Tested migrations in staging first\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Reversible migrations (downgrade path)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Data migration scripts separate from schema\n   \n   ```python\n   # GOOD - Safe migration\n   def upgrade():\n       # Add column with default (fast)\n       op.add_column('students', \n           sa.Column('learning_style', sa.String(50), \n                    server_default='Unknown')\n       )\n       \n       # Create index concurrently (no table lock)\n       op.create_index(\n           'idx_students_learning_style', \n           'students', \n           ['learning_style'],\n           postgresql_concurrently=True\n       )\n   \n   def downgrade():\n       op.drop_index('idx_students_learning_style')\n       op.drop_column('students', 'learning_style')\n   ```\n\n**Output Format**:\n```\nDATABASE OPTIMIZATION REPORT:\n\nPerformance Issues: [count]\n🔴 CRITICAL:\n   - Missing index on students.email (100K+ rows)\n     File: backend/models/user.py:42\n     Impact: Table scan on every login (>5s)\n     Fix: Add index=True to email column\n\n🟠 HIGH:\n   - N+1 query in get_student_dashboard\n     File: backend/api/dashboard.py:78\n     Impact: 50 queries instead of 2\n     Fix: Use joinedload(Student.school)\n\n🟡 MEDIUM:\n   - No connection pool pre-ping\n     File: backend/core/database.py:15\n     Fix: Add pool_pre_ping=True\n\nReplication Status:\n✓ Master-replica configured\n✗ Replication lag: 8.2s (threshold: 5s)\n\nBackup Status:\n✓ Daily backups enabled\n✗ Last restore test: 45 days ago (should be weekly)\n\nMetrics:\n- Cache hit ratio: 87% (target: 95%)\n- Active connections: 12/30\n- Slow queries (>1s): 23 in last 24h\n\nRecommendation: [OPTIMIZE / MONITOR / OK]\n```\n\n**Performance**: < 20 seconds"
  }
}
